---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CliReferenceShell from '../../../components/CliReferenceShell.astro';
import css from '../../../_mock/learning-hub.css?raw';
import lessonCss from '../../../_mock/cli-lesson.css?raw';
import js from '../../../_mock/learning-hub.js?raw';
import main from '../../../_mock/studio-lesson-07-anatomy-of-a-job.main.html?raw';
import { lessonJsonLd } from '../../../data/lesson-jsonld.js';
const article = { headline: "What a Hydra job is made of: four YAML files", description: "Read the four YAML files of a Hydra job, run it, then break it on purpose and read what hdrctl validate reports. Tested with Hydra ETL 0.22.", datePublished: '2026-11-23', dateModified: '2026-11-23', author: 'Bechir Bejaoui' };
const jsonld = lessonJsonLd({
  path: '/cli/guides/anatomy-of-a-job/',
  name: article.headline,
  steps: ["Create a project", "Read the source and the destination", "Read the transformations", "Read the pipeline", "Validate and run the job", "Break it on purpose"],
  faq: [["What files make up a Hydra job?", "A job is a folder with four YAML manifests: sources.yaml, transformations.yaml, destinations.yaml and pipeline.yaml. In the project created by hdrctl init 0.22 the folder is jobs/job1, and it also holds a README.md and a data folder with a sample input.csv."], ["Which manifest is optional?", "transformations.yaml. In our test a job without it validated and ran, and wrote all 3 rows read, where the job with it wrote 2. We removed destinations.yaml in a test and validate reported it as MISSING; we did not test removing the other files."], ["How does pipeline.yaml connect the other files?", "Through ids. pipeline.from names a source declared in sources.yaml, and pipeline.to names a destination declared in destinations.yaml. validate reports an id that is not found and tells you in which file it looked."], ["Where are the paths in a job resolved from?", "In the generated job, the source reads data/input.csv and the destination writes data/output.csv. After a run, output.csv appeared in jobs/job1/data, next to input.csv, so these relative paths start from the job folder."], ["How do I check a job without running it?", "Run hdrctl validate jobs/job1. It checks that each file is present and valid and that pipeline.from and pipeline.to resolve. hdrctl run . --dry-run validates the whole project and runs nothing."]],
  crumbs: [['Get started', '/get-started'], ['Hydra CLI', '/cli/'], ['Guides', '/cli/guides/'], ["Anatomy of a job", '/cli/guides/anatomy-of-a-job/']],
});
---

<BaseLayout title="What a Hydra job is made of" exactTitle="Hydra Job Anatomy: the Four YAML Files | Hydra ETL" description="Read the four YAML files of a Hydra job, run it, then break it on purpose and read what hdrctl validate reports. Tested with Hydra ETL 0.22." article={article} jsonld={jsonld}>
  <style is:global set:html={css}></style>
  <style is:global set:html={lessonCss}></style>
  <CliReferenceShell current="init" guide="anatomy-of-a-job">
    <article class="cli-article cli-guide">
      <Fragment set:html={main} />
    </article>
  </CliReferenceShell>
  <script is:inline set:html={js}></script>
</BaseLayout>

